id: pm-todos-watcher-stability-timer
title: Retry watcher stability sampling when a timer returns early
description: "Existing origin/main CI run 39996955838 failed on Node 26 in test/watcher.test.ts: the installed single-shot watcher returned waiting where queued was expected. watcher.ts waits stableMs once before its final poll; timer wakeup can precede the performance.now stability deadline. This is outside F04/F09 SDK adoption. Evidence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-todos/actions/runs/39996955838/job/120562864191"
type: Task
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[1]: "gh:unbraind/pm-todos#145"
created_at: "2026-10-23T20:43:22.180Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-24T06:23:48.419Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Bound single-shot waiting by the measured stability deadline and verify queued output with a short stability window across supported Node versions.
parent: pm-todos-watcher
comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-23T20:50:19.067Z",codex-agent,Discovered while checking the F04/F09 SDK-adoption release gates. The baseline CI failure is independent of TODO conversion and host transport. Keep this follow-up open; no watcher implementation or coverage thresholds were changed in the SDK task.
  "2026-10-24T06:13:38.671Z",codex-agent,"Claimed issue #145. Source audit: one-shot command assumes a single timer sleep reaches the monotonic threshold; test settle/concurrent helpers and scripts/validate-source-watcher.ts repeat that assumption. Follow mode rechecks on each poll; remaining timers are cancellation, lock-contention or watchdog deadlines. Plan: shared bounded runOnce with injected monotonic clock/timer, budget max(1000 ms, 3 * stableMs), typed still_waiting refusal plus remedy/nonzero command exit; migrate helper assumptions and prove early-wake/change-deadline behavior on real non-git trackers. Use targeted local checks and 200 serial real-timer iterations, then both CI release gates without threshold changes."
  "2026-10-24T06:15:47.013Z",codex-agent,"Regression proof: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"one-shot command rechecks the monotonic clock after early timer wakes\" test/watcher-timing.test.ts passes with the fix (1 pass, 0 fail). Reverting only the one-shot command branch to poll/sleep/poll, retaining the injected clock and all tests, fails exit 1 (0 pass, 1 fail): actual waiting, expected queued at monotonic 0.75 ms. Restored the fix immediately; identical command passes exit 0. Targeted watcher suite passes 19/19, including actual installed CLI without git and SIGTERM persistence. New timing suite passes 4/4, including 200/200 serial real-timer command cycles with persisted proposal checks. Typecheck, test/script typecheck and docstring gate pass (14 files, 89 declarations). No lint script is configured; docstring is the configured source lint gate."
  "2026-10-24T06:17:11.473Z",codex-agent,"Final boundary refinement: runOnce checks its monotonic deadline before every sample, so an overslept timer cannot begin another read after budget expiry. Added an unchanged-source oversleep regression, bringing timing coverage to 5/5 (including 200 serial real-timer cycles); watcher suite 19/19. All five linked commands passed via pm test --run --progress: timing tests, typecheck, test/script typecheck, docstring gate and built watcher suite. Run-result persistence is disabled by existing project policy, so results are recorded here; no policy was changed. Poll interval help now describes both modes. Remaining timers were audited and only bound cancellation/contention/watchdog checks or rechecked polling; no other elapsed-time assumption remains. CI full release gates pending; no thresholds or dependency pins changed."
  "2026-10-24T06:23:46.918Z",codex-agent,"CI full-gate receipt for implementation commit 1e0a763148117afcd0d2c5e686b957aa55754af6: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-todos/actions/runs/40069648146 succeeded. Both npm run release:check and bun run release:check passed on Node 22.18.0 and Node 26: each of four gate executions reported 348 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped, 0 cancelled (1392 total executions), including 200 serial real-timer cycles per gate. All 3 shipped source files were measured. Lines/functions were 99.08/99.48 percent; branches were Node22 npm 94.49, Bun 94.56; Node26 npm 94.56, Bun 94.42. Unchanged thresholds 97/93/98 passed. Canonical-reader and packed-host acceptance, audit, pack, changelog/date and attestation checks passed; both clean CI tracker-health checks passed. Local health diagnostics alone reported extension host-version skew and a generated merge-fence mismatch after restoring incidental install output; these were not product changes and clean CI health is authoritative here. PR ready for review: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-todos/pull/147 . No source changes after this receipt; final metadata-head CI will be checked and linked in the PR. No merge or release performed; item stays in_progress for orchestrator verification. No new PM CLI or SDK defect found."
